  "title": "Ribbon Spool Revenue",
  "description": "## Task\n\nA spool holds `length` centimetres of ribbon. A shop buys pieces of whole centimetre lengths; `prices[k]` is what it pays for one piece of length `k + 1`. You may cut the spool into any number of pieces of any lengths (pieces of one length may repeat) and sell all of them, or leave leftover ribbon unsold. Find the maximum revenue.\n\n## Input\n\n- `length` — the spool length in centimetres.\n- `prices` — non-negative integers; `prices[k]` is the price of a piece of length `k + 1`. Lengths beyond `len(prices)` are not bought.\n\n## Output\n\nThe largest total revenue obtainable.\n\n## Example\n\n```python\nribbon_revenue(8, [1, 5, 8, 9, 10, 17, 17, 20])  # returns 22\nribbon_revenue(5, [3, 1])  # returns 15\nribbon_revenue(0, [4])  # returns 0\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 0 ≤ `length` ≤ 3000\n- 1 ≤ length of `prices` ≤ 3000\n- 0 ≤ each price ≤ 10^6\n",
